  "scope": "Finite-spin product coherent states can pull back the exact prepotential Berry form while failing its gauge-ray identification. Exact polynomial elimination supports a conditional obstruction to a fixed-depth local state preparation with exact linearized gauge rays. A global finite-spin encoding reproduces the Berry form, gauge identification, quadratic energy and prescribed positive mode response. Its spatially nonlocal encoding and inserted spectrum do not derive a local spin phase, nonlinear Einstein gravity or TOE. No Lean theorem."
}
